    "text": "<p>For a reaction, <math><mi>A</mi><mo>⇌</mo><mi>P</mi></math> , the plots of <math><mi> </mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi> </mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> with time at temperatures <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi> </mi><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are given below.<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/hfvjypyvnjrofprcwoemnluhkwpvqmdqzwkmbeapzfebsdgrwp.jpeg\"/><br >If <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>></mo><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> , the correct statement(s) is (are)<br >(Assume <math><mo>∆</mo><msup><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>⊝</mo></mrow></msup><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi> </mi><mo>∆</mo><msup><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>⊝</mo></mrow></msup></math> are independent of temperature and ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mi>K</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi> </mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mo> </mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>K</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi> </mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is greater than <math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></math> . Here H, S , G and K are enthalpy, entropy, Gibbs energy and equilibrium constant, respectively.)</p>",
